message.content:
The issue was that `rich.file_proxy.FileProxy` inherited from `io.TextIOBase`, which provides a default `isatty()` method that always returns `False`. Because of this, `getattr(proxy, "isatty", None)` returned the base class method instead of triggering `__getattr__` to delegate to the wrapped file. This caused `rich.console.Console.is_terminal` to incorrectly return `False` when the output was wrapped in a `FileProxy`, even if the underlying file was a TTY.

To fix this, I explicitly added an `isatty()` method to `FileProxy` that delegates the call to the wrapped file, returning `False` if the wrapped file does not implement `isatty()`.

```python
    def isatty(self) -> bool:
        return getattr(self.__file, "isatty", lambda: False)()
```

